  "markdown": "### \u00a74.2 \u2014 replacement paragraph (\u2264120 words)\n\nSeed variance is not pooled-uniform across the ablation. Per-group sample SDs span 0.07 pp at N=20 to 1.73 pp at N=3 (\u224824\u00d7 range), so we cite the within-plateau pooled SD rather than a single across-experiment number. On the \u03b1=0.75 plateau the pooled SD across N=10 and N=15 is **0.43 pp**, and the N=15 \u2212 N=10 mean Cars gap of **2.87 pp** is highly significant under Welch's t (t=8.19, df=3.04, p=0.0036, Cohen's d=6.69). Cross-plateau \u03b1-ceiling drops dominate within-plateau drift on the first two transitions (N=5\u219210: 9.42 vs 2.91 pp; N=15\u219220: 4.59 vs 2.87 pp), but at N=25\u219230 the drop (1.23 pp) is comparable to drift (1.27 pp), suggesting diminishing returns past N\u224825.\n\n### Table 2 footnote\n\nAt N=3, pushing \u03b1 to 0.95 collapses ImageNet retention to a 3-seed mean of 50.89 pp (individual seeds: 48.63, 51.69, 52.35 pp), 8.36 pp below the 59.25 pp retention threshold; this is why the optimal \u03b1 reverts to 0.50 in row N=3 of Table 2.\n"
